# Local working documents — planning notes, task and fix lists, and the source
# of the deploy branch's full legal text. None of these are project code and
# none belong in a public repo: a *_FIXES.md is a map of what is not fixed yet,
# and LEGAL_HEROKU.md is the www.oiueei.com legal text, which the standalone
# deliberately ships in a generic operator-neutral form instead.
#
# They were only ever protected by .git/info/exclude, which lives inside .git
# and travels with no clone — so on any second machine there was nothing
# stopping them being committed.
#
# `oiueei_*.md` covers the product, deployment, legal and glossary notes that
# live in the author's own documents folder and get copied in here to be worked
# on. They carry the operator's legal identity and the commercial reasoning that
# the public repository deliberately has no version of — and unlike the files
# above, they arrive by a plain `cp`, so nothing about them looks temporary to a
# `git add -A` run three commits later.
*_TASKS.md
*_FIXES.md
LEGAL_HEROKU.md
oiueei_*.md
